            <div xml:id="d185">

                <pb facs="0349" n="239" xml:id="pg239"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860p.512 Residence/10: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Latvia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Sussdorff</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-11-27T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 27,
                                1928—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>69. Your 95, November 22, 10 a.m. Request exemption from tax for American
                    nationals under paragraph 2, Article 1, of the treaty concluded April 20, 1928,
                    which accords national treatment in matters of internal charges or taxes.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
